WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
An electron has a definite
mass and a definite charge.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.760
It hits a screen as a single, tiny impact.

3
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.660
Now fire a beam of electrons
through a thin film of graphite,

4
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.250
a form of carbon.

5
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.020
You might expect a single bright spot.

6
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.820
Instead, the screen shows bright
rings, one inside another.

7
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.140
That is the pattern light
makes when it diffracts.

8
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.050
So how can a particle diffract?

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.670
In this mission, you'll take apart
the tube that makes these rings,

10
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.450
from the hot filament
to the glowing screen.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.740
Then you'll turn up the voltage, and
predict what happens to the rings.

12
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.250
Your mission: explain how
electrons can diffract,

13
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.610
just as light does.
